--- K7 (T-R): a flat rotation curve is not curl-free; the khronon flow is ---
K7 PASS :: (curl v_b)_z = v_c/R; curl(-grad sigma) = 0  a2 (v_tau = v_b where rho_b > 0) has no solution in any rotating disc; c's mean-flow khronon likewise

--- K8 (T-X): an inter-label exchange V(sigma1 - sigma2) ---
K8 PASS :: source in label-1 continuity -Subs(Derivative(V(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, sigma1(z, t) - sigma2(z, t)); label-2 Subs(Derivative(V(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, sigma1(z, t) - sigma2(z, t)); sum 0  total conserved, each label not: where V' != 0 and rho = 0, equal and opposite charges appear (one negative)

--- K9 (a1): baryon-khronon drag -(beta/2) rho_b |v_tau - v_b|^2 enters the khronon equation as a charge flux ---
K9 PASS :: extra term = beta*((v_b(z, t) + Derivative(sigma(z, t), z))*Derivative(rho_b(z, t), z) + (Derivative(sigma(z, t), (z, 2)) + Derivative(v_b(z, t), z))*rho_b(z, t))  d_t rho + d_z[rho v_tau + beta rho_b (v_tau - v_b)] = 0: drag re-routes charge (can create rho < 0 where rho = 0), does not change D v_tau/Dt = -d(Phi - Xi)

